<title>ESTONIA: NOON RADIO HEADLINES - APRIL 2.</title>
<headline>NOON RADIO HEADLINES - APRIL 2.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the headlines on Estonian Kuku radio in the early afternoon. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- Estonian Prime Minister Mart Siimann gave his first press conference on Wednesday.</p>
<p>- Eesti Telefon plans to rise its phone tariffs in May by an average of 12 percent.</p>
<p>- Estonia's trade deficit was 1.2 billion kroons in February, according to customs board statistics.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
